1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,472
The Curiosity Club.

2
00:00:02,472 --> 00:00:05,054
Episode 24.

3
00:00:05,054 --> 00:00:08,002
The Compass and the Stubborn Needle.

4
00:00:08,002 --> 00:00:10,896
Here is something to listen for.

5
00:00:10,896 --> 00:00:15,828
Why did the compass needle change direction when Leo brought a magnet close?

6
00:00:15,828 --> 00:00:17,350
Ready?

7
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:19,456
Let us find out.

8
00:00:19,456 --> 00:00:22,350
The club prepares for a map game.

9
00:00:22,350 --> 00:00:25,883
Maya has a compass, and Leo has a map.

10
00:00:25,883 --> 00:00:30,747
Pip has already marked the snack cupboard as the most important landmark.

11
00:00:30,747 --> 00:00:34,021
Why does the needle keep pointing that way?

12
00:00:34,021 --> 00:00:35,855
he asks.

13
00:00:35,855 --> 00:00:40,624
It responds to Earth's magnetic field, Maya reads from their guide.

14
00:00:40,624 --> 00:00:44,266
One end points roughly toward magnetic north.

15
00:00:44,266 --> 00:00:47,907
Pip rotates the compass case toward the snacks.

16
00:00:47,907 --> 00:00:51,983
The needle turns relative to the case and settles again.

17
00:00:51,983 --> 00:00:54,877
It is very stubborn, he says.

18
00:00:54,877 --> 00:00:58,451
Ms. Park brings two classroom bar magnets.

19
00:00:58,451 --> 00:01:03,410
The children discover that some ends pull together while others push apart.

20
00:01:03,410 --> 00:01:07,404
Opposite magnetic poles attract, she explains.

21
00:01:07,404 --> 00:01:09,619
Like poles repel.

22
00:01:09,619 --> 00:01:12,785
Leo moves a magnet near the compass.

23
00:01:12,785 --> 00:01:15,448
The needle changes direction.

24
00:01:15,448 --> 00:01:17,989
Now it is listening to me!

25
00:01:17,989 --> 00:01:21,997
It is responding to the nearby magnet, Maya says.

26
00:01:21,997 --> 00:01:27,499
That is why we should keep magnetic objects away when using a compass for directions.

27
00:01:27,499 --> 00:01:33,070
They also learn that magnetic north and geographic north are not exactly the same.

28
00:01:33,070 --> 00:01:38,206
For today's simple classroom game, they use their teacher's marked directions.

29
00:01:38,206 --> 00:01:42,391
Pip puts the magnet aside and follows the map properly.

30
00:01:42,391 --> 00:01:45,067
He reaches the reading corner.

31
00:01:45,067 --> 00:01:48,002
No snacks here, he reports.

32
00:01:48,002 --> 00:01:51,807
But there is a book about explorers, says Leo.

33
00:01:51,807 --> 00:01:53,872
Pip chooses it.

34
00:01:53,872 --> 00:02:00,380
A compass can help you find a direction, he concludes, but you still have to decide where you want to go.

35
00:02:00,380 --> 00:02:03,396
Now, a little more to discover.

36
00:02:03,396 --> 00:02:08,749
A compass contains a small magnet that aligns with the surrounding magnetic field.

37
00:02:08,749 --> 00:02:13,682
Nearby magnets and some metal objects can interfere with its direction.

38
00:02:13,682 --> 00:02:18,478
Magnetic north is not identical to the geographic North Pole.

39
00:02:18,478 --> 00:02:22,921
Opposite magnetic poles attract, while like poles repel.

40
00:02:22,921 --> 00:02:25,951
Let us hear the main idea again.

41
00:02:25,951 --> 00:02:30,597
Turning the compass case did not make the needle choose the snack cupboard.

42
00:02:30,597 --> 00:02:34,184
A nearby magnet did change its direction.

43
00:02:34,184 --> 00:02:39,470
The children learned both how a compass helps and why nearby objects can interfere.

44
00:02:39,470 --> 00:02:42,472
Here are three useful expressions.

45
00:02:42,472 --> 00:02:45,516
You can listen, or say them with me.

46
00:02:45,516 --> 00:02:47,826
Which way should we go?

47
00:02:47,826 --> 00:02:50,135
Which way should we go?

48
00:02:50,135 --> 00:02:52,703
Keep the magnet away from it.

49
00:02:52,703 --> 00:02:55,271
Keep the magnet away from it.

50
00:02:55,271 --> 00:02:58,220
The needle points in this direction.

51
00:02:58,220 --> 00:03:01,168
The needle points in this direction.

52
00:03:01,168 --> 00:03:04,035
Remember our listening question?

53
00:03:04,035 --> 00:03:08,967
Why did the compass needle change direction when Leo brought a magnet close?

54
00:03:08,967 --> 00:03:11,154
Here is the answer.

55
00:03:11,154 --> 00:03:15,638
The nearby magnet changed the magnetic field affecting the needle.

56
00:03:15,638 --> 00:03:19,429
And here is a question just for your imagination.

57
00:03:19,429 --> 00:03:24,864
If you made a map of your room, which three landmarks would help someone follow it?

58
00:03:24,864 --> 00:03:28,029
There is more than one possible answer.

59
00:03:28,029 --> 00:03:31,182
Keep wondering, and see you next time.
